# Examples
#
# `examples/apps/*` are the consumer fixture apps — one per documented
# framework/integration target. They are part of the repository: the docs site
# links to them by path (`examples/apps/astro`, …), `pnpm apps:build` and
# `pnpm apps:typecheck` build them, and pnpm-lock.yaml carries one importer per
# app. Ignoring them made all three of those claims false in a fresh clone.
#
# `examples/<feature>/<framework>/` are the canonical concept examples. They are
# part of the repository for the same reason: `/examples` reads their entry file
# by path at build time, `docs:audit:c` typechecks and renders them, and
# `generate-examples.mjs` refuses to run without them. The blanket rule below
# never retired them — they were tracked at 2.0.0-pre despite it, because
# `.gitignore` only stops files being *added*. Deleting the trees in 2.0.0 was
# therefore invisible: nothing showed up as deleted in a fresh checkout, and the
# one gate that reads them reported a missing inventory rather than a regression.
#
# Each concept directory needs its own exception, because a tree that is ignored
# is a tree a contributor cannot add back. Adding a capability means adding one
# line here — `docs:audit:c` fails on an inventory it cannot see, which is the
# guard against forgetting.
#
# Anything else placed directly under `examples/` is an ad-hoc local playground
# and stays untracked.
/examples/*
!/examples/README.md
!/examples/package.json
!/examples/apps/
!/examples/accessibility/
!/examples/basic-theme/
!/examples/cli/
!/examples/custom-scrollbar/
!/examples/devtools/
!/examples/diagnostics/
!/examples/families-modes/
!/examples/history/
!/examples/multi-window-sync/
!/examples/persistence/
!/examples/plugins/
!/examples/provided-themes/
!/examples/runtime/
!/examples/scheduling/
!/examples/scopes/
!/examples/snapshots/
!/examples/sunrise-sunset/
!/examples/theme-generation/
!/examples/theme-scope/
!/examples/themes/
!/examples/tokens/
!/examples/transitions/
!/examples/zero-flash/

# Build output inside the fixture apps that the shared rules above do not cover.
/examples/apps/*/.angular/
/examples/apps/*/.astro/
/examples/apps/*/.svelte-kit/

# repository documentation
!/examples/README.md

# Local tooling state — machine-local
.playwright-mcp/

# Screenshots written by `apps/docs/scripts/shot-badges.mjs` for visual review.
# Checked-in tool, machine-local output: the script exists so the badges can be
# looked at, and the images it produces are read once, not shipped.
/apps/docs/.badges/

# Local redesign scratch space — screenshots, harness pages and pre-redesign
# tarballs kept for visual comparison. Machine-local: referenced by nobody at
# build time, so it is preserved on disk but never committed.
/.redesign-backup/
